  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The development hereby permitted shall be begun before the expiration of three years from the date of this permission.",
    "Condition : 2 - No development shall take place until samples of the materials to be used in the construction of the external surfaces of the hereby permitted have been submitted to and approved in writing by the local planning authority.  Development shall be carried out in accordance with the approved details",
    "Condition : 3 - The proposed development shall be carried out in all respects in accordance with the proposals contained in the application and the plans submitted (Location Plan (Rev.A) and Block Plan (Rev.A) [received on 14 June 2018], and 21954/101/A and 21954/100/- [received on 25 April 2018]) therewith and approved by the Local Planning Authority, or as shall have been otherwise agreed in writing by the Local Planning Authority before the building is used.",
    "Condition : 4 - Notwithstanding the provisions of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development Order) 1995 (or any order revoking or re-enacting that order) no enlargement of the premises or any additional structures/buildings within the curtilage of the site shall be carried out.",
    "Condition : 5 - The windows formed in the side elevation shall be obscure glazed, hinged to open inwards and shall not be repaired or replaced otherwise than with obscured glazing.",
    "Condition : 6 - No additional windows or other glazed openings shall be formed in the walls of the building hereby approved and no additional doors inserted in the building without the prior written consent of the Local Planning Authority.\r\n",
    "Condition : 7 - No demolition or construction work shall take place on the site except between the hours of 8:00am  to 6:00pm on Mondays to Friday and 9 :00am to 1:00pm on Saturdays and none shall take place on Sundays and Public Holidays without the prior agreement of the Local Planning Authority.",
    "Condition : 8 - Prior to first occupation of the development  hereby approved, a detailed plan showing the parking arrangements and hard and soft landscaping to the front of the house must be submitted to and approved in writing by the local planning authority, and these details shall be carried out, as approved, prior to first occupation of the dwelling. The details shall include a pedestrian path to the front door; a porous hardstanding to prevent run-off onto the public highway; a 4.8m deep x 2.4m wide parking space; a low wall or fence measuring no more than 600mm high at either side of the crossover (to minimise harm to neighbouring properties) and soft landscaping details to enhance the street scene.",
    "Condition : 9 - The use hereby permitted shall not be begun until details of the arrangements for storing of waste and recycled materials have been submitted to and approved by the Local Planning Authority.  The arrangements for storing waste and recycled materials shall not be carried out otherwise than in accordance with any approval given and shall be completed before any part of the accommodation hereby permitted is occupied and shall thereafter be retained as such."
  ],
